  "mechanisms": [
    "The human visual system employs a probabilistic strategy, formalized by Bayesian optimal observer theory, to generate visual percepts in response to ambiguous visual stimuli. Perceived distances are biased by the prior probability distributions of physical distances and spatial relationships in typical natural scenes.",
    "The characteristics of human visual space are determined statistically according to the probability distributions of possible stimulus sources, leading to systematic biases in perceived distance when countervailing empirical information is unavailable or altered by context."
  ],
